==Japanese==

===Glyph origin===
{{ja-etym-kokuji}}. Variant form of {{m|ja|錢}} through an intermediate form {{m|ja|𬌩}} obtained by simplifying the right-hand side.<ref>{{R:Wasei Kanji 2014|222}}</ref>

Folk etymology considers it to be a ligature of {{ja-r|文|もん}} and {{ja-r|メ}}, as the unit of distance could also be written as {{ja-r|文%目|もん%め}}.

{{lang|zh|漢典}} (zdic.net) posits the origin as a {{w|regular script}} form of {{ja-r|兩|りょう}}, but this is dubious because the value of the {{m|ja||兩}} was between 4 and 10 ''momme'', and is now either 50g (mainland China) or 37.5g (Taiwan), and of similar value in Hong Kong; i.e., the units are essentially not equivalent.

