====Usage notes====
This character ({{lang|mul|口}}) is used within characters. If a square is used as an enclosure around another character, then the character {{l|mul|囗}} (<code>U+56D7</code>) is used instead.

This radical is sometimes added to characters to indicate that a certain character is onomatopoeic, e.g. {{l|zh|咚}} and {{l|zh|啪|tr=pā}}, or is phonetic, e.g. {{l|zh|咖啡}} and {{l|zh|喇嘛}}.

This radical is also added to measurement units to indicate [[imperial system]] units instead of Chinese traditional units e.g. {{l|zh|呎|t=feet}} vs {{l|zh|尺|t=Chinese feet}}.

